      },
      "text": "Punta Arenas to King George Island"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "05e546a818d99b05e3d86e6357f80ec05bb35f7e8a21c990b5693c976a5dce46",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-51o02k29bbyeytxstzb7f4",
        "model": "GPT-6.1"
      },
      "text": "You’ll be taken from your hotel to Punta Arenas Airport, where the group boards a flight to King George Island in Antarctica.\n\nYour guide will meet you on arrival. The guided tour includes:\n\n- Villa Las Estrellas, the first inhabited settlement;\n- the Russian Orthodox church at Bellingshausen Station;\n- a Zodiac trip to Ardley Island and a visit to its penguin colony;\n- a boat trip to Collins Glacier.\n\nAfter a full day, the group heads to the ice camp on Collins Glacier. The camp is about 5 km, or 6 miles, from the runway.\n\nThe camp has an insulated tent that serves as the group dining room, a separate purpose-built tent housing the main toilet, and three small insulated sleeping units, each for two people.\n\nYou spend the night in Antarctica beside Collins Glacier."
    },
    {
